# The daemon is the base's and the enablement is this module's: `openssh-server`
# stays on every image so a machine is recoverable over the network *if* someone
# turns it on, and no image listens because a Debian postinst said so. The base
# undoes that postinst and `disable ssh.socket` in its own preset keeps
# `preset-all` from re-enabling the socket on a first boot; this is the line
# that opens the service half deliberately.
#
# It sits under `deb/` because the unit is `ssh.service` on both deb families
# and `sshd.service` on Fedora, and that is a family fact rather than a distro
# one. A `fedora/` copy naming `sshd.service` is what adding Fedora costs, once
# `assets/bases.kdl` gives the fedora-bootc row the `provides-file` this module
# requires. That was a `/etc/os-release` branch in `finalize.sh` until
# 2026-09-06, because a preset is applied line by line and a unit that does not
# exist fails the build, so one file could not say two things.
enable ssh.service
